.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Wu&#x27;s 1957 experiment cooled spin-polarized cobalt-60 nuclei and counted emitted electrons above and below the sample: if parity held, electrons should emerge equally often parallel and antiparallel to the nuclear spin. She found instead a pronounced asymmetry, dN/d\cos\theta\propto1+A\cos\theta with A\neq0 -- parity is violated in the weak interaction. This example reproduces exactly that signature using two_body_decay&#x27;s cos_theta parameter: sampling decay angles uniformly (the parity-conserving null hypothesis) gives a flat count-vs-\cos\theta histogram, while weighting the sample by 1+A\cos\theta for A\neq0 reproduces Wu&#x27;s asymmetric distribution directly.">

